 "producing_commit": "4516840d61344c9825719cb0848831363c211c65",
 "reading_the_map": "The ordering column is the point. If the child cut ever crossed the horizon, or the horizon crossed the inner edge, the nesting would have a transition in it. The shift turn moving relative to the excision is the other thing worth watching, because the default excision sits above it for small mu and below it for large ones.",
 "schema": "NSC-RN-GEOMETRY-MAP-v1",
 "scope_note": "A map of one family, not of nested spaces in general. It does not measure the actual universe, and one chart with one child interval is not a hierarchy. What the map can say is whether the ordering of the features is stable as the parameter moves.",
